    "created_at": "2023-10-06T07:20:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-06T07:20:45Z",
    "body": "Powershell does not change the history on empty commands, `Get-History -Count 1` stays the same, and so `src/init/starship.ps1` always gets the same execution time.\r\n\r\nThere is a hack I've used to circumvent this in a custom powershell prompt:\r\nYou can subtract `(Get-History -Count 1).EndExecutionTime` from the current time and not set the duration if the result is above some threshold (I think I used 70ms). That worked _almost_ always.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if that workaround would be acceptable here.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
